Listing 17-13: Using multiple producers with async blocks
First, we clone tx , creating tx1 outside the first async block. We move tx1 into that block
just as we did before with tx . Then, later, we move the original tx into a new async block,
where we send more messages on a slightly slower delay. We happen to put this new async
block after the async block for receiving messages, but it could go before it just as well. The key
is the order in which the futures are awaited, not in which they’re created.
Both of the async blocks for sending messages need to be async move blocks so that both tx
and tx1 get dropped when those blocks finish. Otherwise, we’ll end up back in the same
